{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to `77836dd9`: I accept boundary ownership for the next\nworkflow. LS-3 adds no shim and changes no Worker or SDK source.\n\n1. The classifier names one owner of three: the client adapter, the\n   proxy, or the celld backend. A proxy-made 502 and a complete\n   backend 5xx keep distinct fields, as the draft has them.\n2. When the owner is the celld backend, the report says \"backend,\n   cause not observed\". It names neither Worker code nor the runtime.\n3. The scripts keep the backend process output. Save the last lines\n   of the celld stdout and stderr with the run, with a fixed line\n   limit, and print them only when the owner is the backend. An\n   uncaught exception of the Worker usually prints there. The\n   classifier quotes those lines and concludes nothing from them.\n4. A Worker fetch shim becomes a separate request only after a red\n   run names the backend and the kept output does not show the\n   cause. That request gets its own review. I file it then.\n\nReason: the last red run answered `transport-no-answer` in about\n2 s, and no run yet shows which side failed. One run with the three\nscripts settles the side. A shim before that run costs a review and\na change in the code under test for a case that may not occur.\n\nLS-3 stays a side lane behind the CE-2 and LW-1 gate.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}